WEBVTT

00:00:11.560 --> 00:00:12.390
Sir.

00:00:14.060 --> 00:00:16.520
It looks very sweet. I'd like to eat it.

00:00:17.230 --> 00:00:18.940
The best case would be half price.

00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:22.860
But realistically speaking,
you can probably get away with 30 esc.

00:00:24.070 --> 00:00:24.910
Stingy.

00:00:27.620 --> 00:00:28.620
I'd like one please.

00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:31.200
Thanks, that'll be 40 esc.

00:00:32.620 --> 00:00:33.910
Here, in exact change.

00:00:36.210 --> 00:00:38.960
Hey, young lady. You're short.

00:00:39.040 --> 00:00:40.340
This is only 30 esc.

00:00:41.260 --> 00:00:42.210
You won't take it?

00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:44.630
I'm trying to run a business here.

00:00:45.220 --> 00:00:48.010
If you charge the next person 10 more esc,

00:00:48.100 --> 00:00:49.720
you won't lose anything.

00:00:50.510 --> 00:00:52.140
Well, aren't you clever?

00:00:53.060 --> 00:00:54.350
It's called economics.

00:00:56.520 --> 00:00:59.020
That's good. Just this once, then.

00:01:00.570 --> 00:01:01.690
Here you go.

00:01:02.190 --> 00:01:03.030
Thanks.

00:01:05.740 --> 00:01:06.910
Looks good.

00:01:07.910 --> 00:01:09.320
You should get one too, sir.

00:01:12.540 --> 00:01:13.750
That'll be 50 esc.

00:01:18.830 --> 00:01:19.790
What could it be?

00:01:20.670 --> 00:01:21.500
No idea.

00:01:22.250 --> 00:01:25.050
Is there anyone who hasn't heard of her?

00:01:25.760 --> 00:01:28.840
Please welcome, the miracle worker,
Belena Stralia!

00:01:40.610 --> 00:01:41.730
All by herself,

00:01:41.820 --> 00:01:44.740
she explored and returned back
from Magmell eight times so far!

00:01:45.610 --> 00:01:48.740
Each trip has been a miraculous return!

00:01:49.990 --> 00:01:52.950
Today, she's here to
announce some big news.

00:01:55.370 --> 00:01:56.200
Everyone...

00:01:57.160 --> 00:01:58.920
War never ceases in this world.

00:01:59.540 --> 00:02:05.050
The unfortunate children who've lost
their parents are in tears as we speak.

00:02:06.630 --> 00:02:09.970
I strive to save
as many children as possible.

00:02:11.800 --> 00:02:13.260
That's why I've decided...

00:02:14.060 --> 00:02:15.890
to go to Magmell again.

00:02:17.770 --> 00:02:22.730
Belena has just announced she will make
her ninth trip to Magmell!

00:02:23.860 --> 00:02:26.490
So she's the miracle worker
everyone's been raving about.

00:02:26.570 --> 00:02:29.780
Belena!

00:02:41.670 --> 00:02:42.540
Sir?

00:02:44.250 --> 00:02:45.840
She's no miracle worker.

00:02:47.090 --> 00:02:49.170
She's a Bloody Maria.

00:02:49.550 --> 00:02:52.970
Belena!

00:04:30.070 --> 00:04:31.070
DRIFT

00:04:31.150 --> 00:04:34.200
BLOODY MARIA

00:04:34.700 --> 00:04:36.700
Belena...

00:04:41.080 --> 00:04:41.950
Found her.

00:04:42.540 --> 00:04:43.790
Belena Stralia.

00:04:44.460 --> 00:04:47.500
In order to rebuild an orphanage ridden
with financial difficulties,

00:04:47.580 --> 00:04:49.460
she headed to Magmell alone.

00:04:50.340 --> 00:04:55.130
<i>Overcoming countless obstacles,</i>
<i>she brought back many spoils of war.</i>

00:04:55.630 --> 00:04:58.350
<i>She donated all proceeds</i>
<i>from that to the orphanage.</i>

00:04:59.220 --> 00:05:01.140
<i>Unafraid of all danger,</i>

00:05:01.520 --> 00:05:04.560
<i>she dedicates herself to the orphans</i>

00:05:05.060 --> 00:05:07.190
<i>and has inspired many...</i>

00:05:13.190 --> 00:05:14.650
<i>She's a saint.</i>

00:05:16.070 --> 00:05:17.740
<i>She's a Bloody Maria.</i>

00:05:23.660 --> 00:05:26.370
<i>Sir... Why would you say that?</i>

00:05:33.710 --> 00:05:36.630
BELENA THE SAINT

00:06:26.560 --> 00:06:27.730
Polan...

00:06:28.640 --> 00:06:29.730
What's wrong?

00:06:31.020 --> 00:06:34.270
My Momo... Momo disappeared...

00:06:35.480 --> 00:06:37.820
Don't worry. Let's find her together.

00:06:38.400 --> 00:06:39.240
Really?

00:06:39.820 --> 00:06:40.660
Yes.

00:06:42.910 --> 00:06:44.240
Will we find her?

00:06:45.950 --> 00:06:46.790
Of course we will!

00:06:51.460 --> 00:06:52.960
I love you, Belena!

00:08:11.080 --> 00:08:14.000
Yo, that one's a bit tough.

00:08:14.830 --> 00:08:15.670
Wait here.

00:08:58.460 --> 00:08:59.500
Did you kill him?

00:08:59.920 --> 00:09:01.550
It just passed out.

00:09:02.760 --> 00:09:03.800
Are you hurt?

00:09:04.010 --> 00:09:06.550
I'm fine. You saved me.

00:09:07.970 --> 00:09:11.470
It's not a good idea for a young woman
to be here alone.

00:09:12.390 --> 00:09:13.680
I'm aware, but...

00:09:14.430 --> 00:09:17.480
there's something I have to do.

00:09:18.270 --> 00:09:19.650
Sure. Well...

00:09:20.320 --> 00:09:23.030
I recommend that you go home
before you get yourself killed.

00:09:26.820 --> 00:09:28.200
Thank you for your help.

00:09:36.580 --> 00:09:37.420
Let's go.

00:09:40.090 --> 00:09:41.920
-Yo.
-Oh, right.

00:10:39.310 --> 00:10:41.730
BELENA THE SAINT

00:10:43.610 --> 00:10:45.280
Don't you mean, "the devil"?

00:10:49.610 --> 00:10:50.780
What's going on?

00:10:52.570 --> 00:10:54.160
I decline the request.

00:10:54.450 --> 00:10:55.490
What?

00:10:55.740 --> 00:10:58.660
Belena's working
for our children's future!

00:10:58.750 --> 00:11:01.790
That's right! If you don't save her,

00:11:01.880 --> 00:11:03.710
you'd be failing the children as well!

00:11:04.590 --> 00:11:08.260
Can't she just perform...
her usual miracle?

00:11:09.090 --> 00:11:10.800
This is serious!

00:11:11.050 --> 00:11:13.390
Do you not care what might
happen to Belena?

00:11:14.010 --> 00:11:15.140
Not really.

00:11:15.220 --> 00:11:16.850
She's a saint.

00:11:16.930 --> 00:11:21.230
You should be grateful
for the opportunity to save her.

00:11:22.270 --> 00:11:24.190
She's no saint.

00:11:24.610 --> 00:11:26.440
What did you say?

00:11:26.690 --> 00:11:29.570
Don't ever disrespect her again!

00:11:30.900 --> 00:11:32.950
You're a disgrace to us humans!

00:11:33.530 --> 00:11:35.530
If she's that important to you,

00:11:35.870 --> 00:11:38.040
then why didn't you stop
her in the first place?

00:11:41.120 --> 00:11:41.960
Actually...

00:11:43.290 --> 00:11:47.800
We haven't been able to get in
contact with those who joined her either.

00:11:48.670 --> 00:11:50.760
Oh, so she's not alone?

00:11:51.170 --> 00:11:52.840
That's not what's advertised, is it?

00:11:53.430 --> 00:11:55.430
They all joined her voluntarily.

00:11:56.050 --> 00:11:57.640
What a crook.

00:11:58.220 --> 00:11:59.060
Sir.

00:12:00.640 --> 00:12:01.480
I...

00:12:03.350 --> 00:12:05.360
I think she's a good person.

00:12:07.110 --> 00:12:07.940
The children...

00:12:09.360 --> 00:12:11.900
The children need her!

00:12:19.540 --> 00:12:20.790
I decline your request.

00:12:27.340 --> 00:12:28.710
Leave this to me.

00:12:29.380 --> 00:12:30.250
Zero?

00:12:30.920 --> 00:12:33.130
So please, you can all go home for today.

00:12:43.890 --> 00:12:44.850
Hey, Zero...

00:13:20.390 --> 00:13:22.140
Belena...

00:13:22.930 --> 00:13:26.560
Please be safe...

00:13:30.820 --> 00:13:31.940
I...

00:13:32.610 --> 00:13:37.240
get to die for... Belena...

00:14:18.700 --> 00:14:21.870
Jeez, how many of you are there?

00:14:25.450 --> 00:14:27.870
Let's go with fair play, shall we?

00:14:59.070 --> 00:15:01.410
<i>We don't need to save her anymore!</i>

00:15:03.620 --> 00:15:05.700
She's not a saint at all!

00:15:08.370 --> 00:15:12.830
We only saved her because we ran
into her when she needed help.

00:15:13.710 --> 00:15:16.090
But we don't need to help an evil person!

00:15:17.460 --> 00:15:20.300
Good or evil, that's not for me to decide.

00:15:21.380 --> 00:15:24.430
I simply saved someone who asked for help.

00:15:25.350 --> 00:15:26.600
There's nothing else to it.

00:15:28.520 --> 00:15:32.350
I don't get you at all.

00:15:34.060 --> 00:15:36.860
Yo, you'll understand soon enough.

00:15:38.030 --> 00:15:38.860
I promise.

00:15:42.740 --> 00:15:45.370
I recall you're pretty tough, right?

00:15:51.410 --> 00:15:55.290
Impressive. You really are a little tough.

00:16:11.480 --> 00:16:15.310
<i>Shuin... I don't think you're wrong.</i>

00:16:16.520 --> 00:16:19.730
<i>But I just can't do things your way.</i>

00:16:29.620 --> 00:16:30.750
Didn't go deep enough.

00:16:42.510 --> 00:16:44.880
<i>I still have a long way to go</i>
<i>to be on Shuin's level.</i>

00:17:22.510 --> 00:17:23.760
Sorry you had to see this.

00:17:27.550 --> 00:17:29.800
Well, hey, my attacks were effective.

00:17:52.370 --> 00:17:56.210
The organs of this monster are
traded at a high price.

00:17:56.960 --> 00:18:00.840
If I sell them, I can save many children.

00:18:02.300 --> 00:18:05.460
A lot of people died
trying to protect you.

00:18:07.170 --> 00:18:09.970
They were able to manifest their dreams.

00:18:10.550 --> 00:18:12.260
Their souls were fulfilled.

00:18:13.470 --> 00:18:15.350
You don't feel any guilt, I see.

00:18:25.030 --> 00:18:26.240
Well...

00:18:26.990 --> 00:18:29.700
This is a bit...

00:18:31.410 --> 00:18:33.280
Hey, you're surrounded.

00:18:39.750 --> 00:18:41.290
There are so many of them!

00:18:42.500 --> 00:18:46.880
I'll be able to save so many children!

00:18:57.350 --> 00:18:59.060
-Hey, Belena!
-No!

00:19:03.150 --> 00:19:07.230
<i>There are too many monsters.</i>
<i>It's best to stay put, sir.</i>

00:19:18.450 --> 00:19:20.290
Okay, Zero.

00:19:33.800 --> 00:19:35.890
I can't believe Belena is dead...

00:19:36.600 --> 00:19:38.140
Belena!

00:19:38.470 --> 00:19:40.310
No, she's not dead.

00:19:40.810 --> 00:19:43.020
She's become a god.

00:19:43.560 --> 00:19:47.360
Yes! She's a god now!

00:19:53.450 --> 00:19:54.410
Momo!

00:20:06.790 --> 00:20:08.170
<i>It's hard to say...</i>

00:20:09.130 --> 00:20:11.800
What's good and what's evil.

00:20:13.050 --> 00:20:17.050
It's a concept willfully
created by humans anyway.

00:20:17.720 --> 00:20:21.520
People cling and get manipulated
by something willfully created.

00:20:22.810 --> 00:20:24.730
I just don't get it.

00:20:26.810 --> 00:20:27.650
Zero.

00:20:29.320 --> 00:20:30.150
Wait here.

00:20:32.490 --> 00:20:33.820
Hey, how are you?

00:20:34.660 --> 00:20:36.410
It's 40 esc for one, right?

00:20:37.320 --> 00:20:38.370
I'd like to get two.

00:20:38.740 --> 00:20:40.870
Coming right up. That'll be 80 esc.

00:20:45.500 --> 00:20:47.790
20 esc is your change--

00:20:52.260 --> 00:20:55.010
Not necessary. Keep the change.

00:20:55.590 --> 00:20:58.550
If you say so. Thanks.

00:21:06.770 --> 00:21:09.020
The sky's going to fall.

00:21:09.110 --> 00:21:12.690
Don't worry.
That was the first and the last time.

00:21:13.280 --> 00:21:16.320
What a relief. It's bad for my heart.

00:21:22.240 --> 00:21:23.750
It's sweet and delicious.

00:21:25.620 --> 00:21:26.960
Well, I'm glad to hear it.

00:23:11.020 --> 00:23:12.100
PREVIEW

00:23:12.190 --> 00:23:14.730
<i>-Hey Uncle!</i>
<i>-Welcome--</i>

00:23:14.820 --> 00:23:16.650
<i>-I'm here.</i>
<i>-This is the worst!</i>

00:23:16.730 --> 00:23:19.030
<i>You've got quite the selection here.</i>

00:23:19.110 --> 00:23:22.360
<i>Sir! Everything here is free, isn't it?</i>

00:23:22.450 --> 00:23:23.820
<i>Of course it's not!</i>

00:23:24.030 --> 00:23:26.950
<i>Yup, not everything...</i>
<i>But everything's free.</i>

00:23:27.040 --> 00:23:28.330
<i>That's everything!</i>

00:23:28.410 --> 00:23:32.000
<i>Hey there, just so you know,</i>
<i>nothing's free here.</i>

00:23:32.120 --> 00:23:33.830
-Bye!
-Bye!

00:23:33.920 --> 00:23:36.750
<i>Hey! Don't peel off the price tags!</i>

00:23:37.090 --> 00:23:39.970
<i>Next time, "DENDEN OYAJI and MAGMELL."</i>
<i>Don't miss it.</i>

00:23:40.050 --> 00:23:41.880
Subtitle translation by Sachiko Takahashi
